//   6. Per-backend early dispatches (thread/start|resume|fork|turn/start):
//      auggieBackendRequested -> auggieBridgeFor + configureAuggieUpstream;
//      clineBackendRequested -> clineBridgeFor + configureClineUpstream;
//      commandCodeBackendRequested -> commandCodeBridgeFor + configureCommandCodeUpstream;
//      claude -> resolveClaudeBridgeForThread (managed config dir / ssh launcher);
//      thread/compact/start with claudeBridge -> claude bridge request.
//   7. thread/list: historyBackendScope assembly — merge per-backend list results
//      (miniThreadListResult, claudeThreadListResult, agyThreadListResult,
//      grokThreadListResult, museThreadListResult, piThreadListResult,
//      opencodeThreadListResult(ownerId, backend), cline/commandCode/auggie async
//      list results) + mergeSshWorkspaceThreads + annotateSshThreadResult;
//      cursor-based paging branch when params.cursor present (native codex list).
//   8. thread/fork: metadataOnlyFork (params.__codexUltraNoTurns === true) ->
//      metadata clone path; else bridge fork + roster/metadata carry-over.
//   9. History reads: thread/history/fileInfo + thread/history/tail routed per
//      backend flag matrix (see source ternaries): local -> threadHistoryFileInfo /
//      threadHistoryTail(bridge, params) with DEFAULT_HISTORY_TAIL_BYTES;
//      restoreLegacyImageViewsForRpc post-processing on thread/read|resume|
//      turns/list|items/list results; stripThreadTurns for summary reads.
//   10. fs/readFile | fs/writeFile: when SSH profile -> ssh bridge; when
//      non-codex runtime bridge or specific backends (agy/grok/pi/opencode/mini)
//      -> local RPC fns (readLocalWorkspaceFileRpc / writeLocalWorkspaceFileRpc
//      via expandFilesystemRpcParams); else native bridge fs request.
//   11. Claude host skills: isClaudeHostSkillRpc(method) -> handleClaudeHostSkillRpc;
//      turn/start for claude -> expandClaudeSkillTurnInput rewrite.
//   12. Dynamic tools / sa_vm: parseDynamicToolArguments for dynamic tool calls;
//      turn/start with vmEnabled (params or runtime) -> validateSaVmRequestBody +
//      policy-attached params; sa_vm tool results via runSaVmTool dispatch
